{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": -400,
      "width": 2340,
      "height": 100,
      "text": "# Epistack — current implementation · data flow & stores\nHow data is structured (**stores**) and how it moves (**labeled edges**). Straight from the `claude/work` tree · updated 2026-07-20."
    },
    {
      "id": "legend",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": -270,
      "width": 1480,
      "height": 90,
      "text": "🟦 human input · 🟪 backend endpoint (`claude -p`) · 🟩 store / data structure · 🟨 rendered view · 🟥 open gap · ✅ closed gap. **⟨WebSearch⟩** = hits the live internet."
    },
    {
      "id": "beknote",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1580,
      "y": -270,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 130,
      "text": "**Backend** = 11 vite dev-middleware routes, each spawns **`claude -p`** (free, no API key): decompose · personalize · suggest · research⟨web⟩ · deepdive⟨web⟩(two-phase) · plan(legacy) · **compile** · dependence · matrix · decide · prompts. Model picker ⚙ appends `--model`; every call logged → terminal + `epistack.log`.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "g1",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -40,
      "y": -120,
      "width": 2520,
      "height": 580,
      "label": "STAGE 1 · EXPAND"
    },
    {
      "id": "in_q",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 170,
      "text": "**textarea `question`**\n`tokenize()` → `tokens[]`\n(⌘↵ → decompose; re-asking a saved question = instant full restore)",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_dec",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 210,
      "text": "**POST `/api/decompose`**\nfn `decomposePrompt(question, tokens)`\ntools: — · `claude -p`\n\n⚖️ prior-conflation fix: resolutions stay NEUTRAL; the AI's tentative answer goes in a separate `prior` field, kept OUT of the research agents.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_data",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": -60,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 330,
      "text": "**`data`**  (persisted · localStorage `epistack_investigations[question]` + decompose cache)\n`{ clusters:[{ id, name, color, prompt,\n    resolutions[] (neutral candidates),\n    prior (explicit, to-be-tested),\n    highlightQuotes[] (verbatim spans of the question; MANY-TO-MANY — one word may ground several dimensions) }],\n  elicit:[{id, question, why, options[]}] }`\n\n`assignments[]` is GONE — per-token membership is computed client-side: `computeTokenMembers(tokens, clusters)` → per-token cluster SETS.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_cluster",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": -20,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "**Stage-1 `expand-layout`** (two-column)\nleft **q-rail**: pinned question, per-token multi-membership colors + numbered dimension nav\nright **ClusterDetail**: auto-growing editable name/prompt/resolutions · \"grounded in your words\" cues · AI-prior chip · ✨ suggest → `/api/suggest`",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g2",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -40,
      "y": 540,
      "width": 2520,
      "height": 560,
      "label": "STAGE 2 · CONTEXTUALIZE"
    },
    {
      "id": "in_ctx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 190,
      "text": "**`elicitAns{qid:opt}`** (chips)\n+ **`ctxText`** (free-text rant)\n\nsaved live as you type — no re-entry on return",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_pers",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 190,
      "text": "**POST `/api/personalize`**\nfn `personalizePrompt(question, clusters, context)`\ntools: — · `claude -p`",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_pdata",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 290,
      "text": "**`pdata`** (persisted) + **`ctxSummary`** (rant + \"Q → A\" lines, joined)\n`{ clusters:[{ id, status: pinned|open|dropped, value, reason }],\n  newClusters:[{id, name, color, prompt, resolutions[], reason}],\n  takeaway }`\n\npinned = your context answers it → applicability FACT\nopen = still uncertain FOR YOU → research lane\ndropped = irrelevant to you → parked, zero budget",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_pmap",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 190,
      "text": "**PersonalizedMap**\n\"for you, it comes down to\" takeaway + settled-by-you / worth-investigating / new-for-you / skip cards",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -40,
      "y": 1180,
      "width": 2520,
      "height": 2780,
      "label": "STAGE 3 · RESEARCH + ENRICH  (ResearchStage)"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_axes",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1280,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "**`axes`** (computed)\n`pdata ? [openClusters… , newClusters…] : data.clusters`\n← the *filtered graph*: only what your context left OPEN gets research budget",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_cmp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 1540,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "**POST `/api/compile`**  ★ NEW — the research compiler\nfn `compilePrompt(question, context, pinned, dropped, axes)`\ntools: — · `claude -p` (240s window, ~157s observed)\n\nProjects Stage 1×2 into a tractable plan: claim portfolio + applicability profile + retrieval plans + parked. Subsumes the `/api/plan` orchestrator (route kept as legacy).",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_brief",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1500,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 360,
      "text": "**`brief`** (persisted in the research slice) — the RESEARCH BRIEF\n`{ applicability:[{ field: population|dose|comparator|outcome|setting|implementation, value, use: constrain-search | judge-transport-only }],\n  claims:[{ id, axis, priority, kind: effectiveness|harm|comparator|mechanism|implementation, statement (scoped PICO), population, intervention, comparator, outcome, wouldChange, queries[] (privacy-scrubbed), sources, relaxation[] (constraint ladder) }],\n  parked:[{axis, name, reactivate}],\n  privacyNote }`\n\n3–7 claims TOTAL; every open axis covered or explicitly parked.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_brief",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 1540,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "**research-brief panel**\napplicability chips (dashed = transport-only, kept OUT of searches) · claim cards: P# priority, kind, PICO row, \"would change the decision\", outbound queries, relaxation ladder · parked rows · 🔒 privacy note · ↻ recompile",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_res",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 1940,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "**POST `/api/research`** ⟨WebSearch+WebFetch⟩\nfn `researchPrompt(axis, context, claims, applicability, brief)`\n`claude -p --allowedTools WebSearch,WebFetch` (~60-360s)\n\nAgents research the CLAIM FRAMES, climb the relaxation ladder one constraint at a time, and score every finding's scope distance. 🔒 outbound queries must never carry identifying details.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_lanes",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1930,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "**`lanes`** (persisted when done · key `axisId`)\n`{ status, t0, ms, findings:[{\n   claim, supports, source, url, kind, n, year,\n   confidence, coi, dataset,\n   claimId? (which compiled claim it bears on),\n   scope?:{population, dose, comparator, outcome: match|near|far},\n   scopeNote? (which constraint was relaxed),\n   relevance? }] }`",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_graph",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 1960,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 230,
      "text": "**GraphState** — evidence-spread bars + verdict\n**ResearchLane** — live status/timer/findings\n**FindingCard** — provenance tags + NEW scope-match chips (match ◆ / near / far △)",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_stats",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 2290,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "**`statsById`** = `axisStats(axis, findings)`\n`{ segs, u = normalised entropy, evidence, top }`\n⚠ **spread of retrieved findings, NOT P(truth)**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_dd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 2510,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "**POST `/api/deepdive`** ⟨WebSearch+WebFetch⟩ · TWO-PHASE\n1️⃣ `deepDiveEnumeratePrompt` — find the paper, list result stubs\n2️⃣ `deepDiveDetailPrompt` — chunked detail per stub\n(carved along natural boundaries after the monolithic call kept truncating; tolerant JSON + timeout + one retry)",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_ledg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 2490,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "**`ledgers`** (persisted · key `axisId#idx`)  ← *canonical result store*\n`{ study:{design, journal, journal_tier, peer_reviewed, investigators, funding, coi, open_data, dataset, critiques},\n  results:[{ statement, locus, population, exposure, outcome, estimate, model, status, n, relation (supports|qualifies|undercuts…), relationNote, verification: source-checked|abstract-only|review-extracted|unverified }],\n  authorConclusion:{text, assessment} }`\n\na paper is a CONTAINER — one source ≠ one vote",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_ledg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 2540,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**ResultLedger** — result cards with relation/status/**verification** chips + passage `locus`; author-conclusion flagged when it outruns the results",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_dep",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 2880,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "**POST `/api/dependence`**\nfn `dependencePrompt(findings)`\ntools: — · `claude -p` (~17s)",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_fam",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 2860,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 210,
      "text": "**`families`** (persisted · key `axisId`)\n`{ families:[{id, label, basis, members[], note}],\n  independentCount, totalSources, note }`\n\nshared cohort/team/data = ONE family — counts once",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_dep",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 2890,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "**DependencePanel** — 'N sources → K independent families'; correlated evidence flagged amber",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_mat",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 3140,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 190,
      "text": "**POST `/api/matrix`**\nfn `matrixPrompt(sources — result-aware)`\ntools: — · `claude -p` (~50s)",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_mat",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 3120,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "**AxisMatrix `m`** (component-local · transient)\n`{ sources:[{id, name, url, deepDived}],\n  claims:[{id, text, resolution}],\n  cells:[{claim, source, verdict: supports|disputes|qualifies|mixed|silent, results:[\"statement → relation\"]}] }`",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_mat",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 3150,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "**claim × source matrix** (toggle) — cells show verdict + the result statements behind it",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "note_a2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 3400,
      "width": 1300,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "✅ **A.2 CLOSED** — the matrix is now a PROJECTION over result-level evidence: deep-dived sources carry `results[]` into `/api/matrix`, cells reason per-result (supports/disputes/**qualifies/mixed**/silent). A paper with 8 results is no longer squashed back into one vote.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "ep_dcd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 3600,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**POST `/api/decide`**\nfn `decidePrompt(question, context, applicability, dimensions)`\ntools: — · `claude -p` (~60s)\n\nreasons at the RESULT level · prefers source-checked · counts FAMILIES not sources · weighs scope distance via the applicability profile",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_dcn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 3610,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**`decision`** (persisted in the research slice)\n`{ answer, stance, for[], against[], crux,\n  decisiveTest (n=1 experiment + what it can't settle),\n  confidence, confidenceNote, missing[] }`",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_dcd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1940,
      "y": 3620,
      "width": 440,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "**decision panel** — answer/stance/for·against/crux/n=1 test/confidence/missing",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g4",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -40,
      "y": 4040,
      "width": 2520,
      "height": 480,
      "label": "STAGE 4 · ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_art",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 4160,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "**Stage4Artifact** (step 4 in the stepper)\nreads the WHOLE persisted investigation: the takeaway, every dimension's fate (settled-by-your-context / researched with finding+result counts / parked), the evidence families, and the decision — the navigable record of what was asked, what your context pruned, what the agents found, and what it all settled.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "g5",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -40,
      "y": 4600,
      "width": 2520,
      "height": 720,
      "label": "PERSISTENCE + EXPORT  (cross-cutting)"
    },
    {
      "id": "st_store",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 4720,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 340,
      "text": "✅ **A.3 CLOSED** — **localStorage `epistack_investigations[question]`**\n`{ data, tokens, pdata, context, elicitAns, ctxText, step,\n  research:{ lanes(done only), plan(legacy), brief, ledgers, families, decision },\n  interactions:[ every human action + AI call via logInteraction ] }`\n\nsaved live as state changes; re-asking the SAME question (exact string) restores everything instantly — chips, rant, brief, findings, step. Plus `epistack_model` (⚙ model pref) and `epistack_decomp_cache`.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "vw_exp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1420,
      "y": 4740,
      "width": 540,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "**⤓ export** — one JSON with EVERYTHING: question, decomposition, context (rant + answers), research slice (findings, ledgers, families, brief, decision), and the human interaction log. AI data + human data, schema-versioned.\n\n**⚙ settings** → model picker + **prompt inspector** (`/api/prompts`, all 12 prompts with «placeholder» inputs — view-only).",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "gap_open",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520,
      "y": 5100,
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 160,
      "text": "⚠ **STILL OPEN:** prompt EDITING (inspector is view-only) · single-provider (100% `claude -p` subagents — no Exa/Grok/Gemini fan-out) · no gap-agent feedback loop (`decision.missing` doesn't reactivate Stage 2 or ask a targeted follow-up) · scope-match vector recorded at research level only (deep-dive results carry `population` but no match scoring) · cache keyed on the EXACT question string (no fuzzy match)",
      "color": "1"
    }
  ],
